        "type": "Module",
        "name": "dac_control",
        "description": "MCP4725 is a single-channel 12-bit I2C DAC powered from VCC_3V3 and controlled by the MCU over the shared I2C bus. Its VOUT provides the analog bias/control voltage that feeds the NE5532 channel-1 non-inverting input network through downstream passive conditioning. The A0 pin must be set to a defined logic/address state in downstream wiring because the part exposes address selection in the provided pin data. This module does not own I2C pull-up policy; it only joins the shared bus as a slave device.",
